.SS Pager Hierarchy
\f[CR]$PAGER\f[R] is set to \f[CR]ov\f[R] when available, falling back
to \f[CR]less\f[R].
The \f[CR]less\f[R] wrapper function extends this into a full chain so
anything that calls \f[CR]less\f[R] directly also benefits:
.PP
\f[CR]$PAGER\f[R] → \f[CR]ov\f[R] → \f[CR]less\f[R] → \f[CR]more\f[R] →
\f[CR]cat\f[R]
.PP
When \f[CR]bat\f[R] is installed, man pages are rendered with syntax
highlighting:
